  "section_notes": "The final S2 has no numeric permanent limit and no sales stop: a 5% failure rate only triggers notice, a corrective-action plan and retesting, which favours Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S3 gives a 6-year retrofit window, also favouring Northwind given its 38% shut-off coverage. S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100k with no transition, which bites on Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), though it does not require a market ban; S4's 36-month suppression deadline favours Halcyon."
